4. PROJECT CREATION

The package consumer should initialize/register a project using a unique project name.

Example:

initializeBackend({
  project: {
    name: 'therapist',
  },
  ...
});

The package must create or resolve a unique:

project_id

for that project.

The generated project_id must then be used as the tenant/project reference for users and other package-owned entities.

Example:

project
   │
   └── project_id
          │
          ├── users
          ├── password reset records
          ├── sessions/tokens
          └── other package-owned records

Do NOT use project name as the database foreign key.

Use a stable unique ID.

Project name/slug can be changed later without breaking references.

5. PROJECT ISOLATION

Every user MUST belong to a project.

User records must contain:

project_id

The package must ensure that users from one project cannot access users from another project.

Every user-related query must be project-aware.

Example:

project A
    ↓
user A1
user A2

project B
    ↓
user B1
user B2

A request authenticated under project A must NEVER be able to access:

user B1
user B2

unless explicitly authorized through a future cross-project administrative mechanism.

Do not rely only on frontend filtering.

Project isolation must be enforced at the backend/service/repository level.

